Poodle Earth is a small, fast globe and atlas for the X Window System.
Drag to turn the globe, zoom in to coastlines, borders, terrain and
cities. It was written to run on modest hardware, including 1990s-2000s
PowerPC machines, and draws everything itself with plain Xlib: no GTK,
Qt, OpenGL or network access.

The maps, elevation and place names are built into the executable, so no
data files are installed and nothing is written to your home directory.
The program is GPL-3.0-or-later; the data is separate and keeps its own
licences (see DATA-CREDITS.txt in the documentation directory).
